{
 "schema": "scratchbox.tree-textures/1",
 "about": "Surface textures for staged trees, chosen per tree by appearance (measured crown colour, leaf size, trunk size) and tinted to measured colour. Entries are described by continuous quantities only; the appearance text is for a model to read and is never branched on.",
 "conventions": {
  "colour": "meanLinearRgb / spreadLinearRgb: mean and standard deviation of linear sRGB (Rec. 709 primaries, D65) over the opaque pixels (leaves) or all pixels (bark); meanLab / spreadLab: CIELAB (D65) of the same pixels; meanLuminance: Rec. 709 Y.",
  "uv": "UV origin at the bottom-left of the image, v up (a texture loaded with flipY). A leaf cell maps leaf-local (s across, t along; base at t = 0) to uv = origin + t * along + s * across, s and t in [0, 1]; the blade starts at the stalk's attachment (the stalk itself is outside the cell).",
  "leafSize": "Estimated: an atlas's longer side is taken to span 0.40 m (the leaves' sizes relative to each other are as scanned; the absolute scale is an estimate from typical leaf proportions).",
  "barkSize": "Estimated: a bark scan's shorter side is taken to span 0.50 m (the smooth scan shows the trunk's curvature across its width, about one trunk diameter). x runs around the trunk, y along it.",
  "barkRelief": "displacementRange: robust range (2.5-97.5 %) of the displacement map high-passed at 4 cm (the trunk's own curvature removed), in the map's normalised units; normalSlopeMean: mean slope |n_xy| / n_z of the normal map; reliefIndex = displacementRange x normalSlopeMean (0 smooth .. about 0.5 deeply furrowed); ridgeSpacingM: dominant period across the trunk (1.5-25 cm) of the high-passed displacement; furrowDepthM: estimated as normalSlopeMean x ridgeSpacingM / 4 (a triangular ridge profile).",
  "coverage": "coverage: opaque share of the whole atlas; leaf.fill: median share of a leaf cell's box the leaf covers.",
  "bladeWidth": "leaf.bladeWidthM: the width of the leaf's flat parts, twice its opaque area over its outline's length (the outline counted in pixel edges times pi / 4), the median over the atlas cells: a broad leaf's blade, a needle spray's branchlets and scale leaves. Measured by scripts/measure_tree_leaf_blades.py."
 },
